WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.970 --> 00:00:05.590
- All right, Selena.
Selena where'd you grow up?

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:06.880
Where are you from originally?

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:08.610
- Here in Manchester.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.890
- And tell me about your family,
you had both your parents

00:00:11.890 --> 00:00:14.187
growing up or do you have
both your parents currently?

00:00:14.187 --> 00:00:15.253
- No.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:17.480
- What do you mean?

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:22.480
- My mother, she's a drug
addict. She had four kids and

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.623
let us all get adopted
by parts of the family.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.830
- Oh really? So you've been adopted?

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:30.663
- Yes.

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:36.820
- And how is your adopted family?

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.897
- My adopted family still..

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.900
how do I put this?

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:43.853
Hold on I'm sorry.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:51.670
My adopted family is my family already.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:54.920
But my aunt is no longer
my aunt. She's my mom.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.190
- Oh I see, so your aunt became your mom?

00:00:57.190 --> 00:00:58.023
- Yes.

00:00:58.023 --> 00:01:00.655
- Okay I got it. And is your
biological mom still around?

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.660
- She's in and out. But when she's around,

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.530
she's not the best.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:06.363
- Oh I see.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.403
So how would you describe your childhood?

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:13.810
It seems like you're having
a nice happy childhood right?

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:17.880
- Yeah. But like when I was
little, you know, I would

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.860
go around my real mom but it just

00:01:20.860 --> 00:01:23.610
wasn't good for me as being a little kid

00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:25.270
seeing that growing up.

00:01:25.270 --> 00:01:26.490
- Seeing what? The drugs?

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.652
- Yes.

00:01:27.652 --> 00:01:29.650
- You know, I've interviewed
some other members of

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.050
your family and there seems like drugs are

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:33.230
pretty vivid.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:34.063
- Plenty.

00:01:34.063 --> 00:01:35.780
- All through clay
county there's drugs but

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:39.050
your families no exception.
So its all around you.

00:01:39.050 --> 00:01:40.870
You're in high school right now?

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:41.703
- Yes.

00:01:41.703 --> 00:01:43.062
- What year are you in high school?

00:01:43.062 --> 00:01:44.067
- I'm in 11th grade.

00:01:44.067 --> 00:01:48.010
- So you have one more year.
And how do you navigate

00:01:48.010 --> 00:01:52.453
the fact that there are
drugs all over your house?

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.053
- I just try to stay away
from it the best I can.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.540
For me, I don't see that as a lifestyle.

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.820
I see it as a choice that somebody makes

00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:06.650
and its really broke my
family apart to be honest.

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.320
- Yeah, its very destructive.

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:09.330
- Yes

00:02:09.330 --> 00:02:10.891
Do you have friends in school that are

00:02:10.891 --> 00:02:12.963
playing around with drugs aw well?

00:02:12.963 --> 00:02:14.560
- Yes.

00:02:14.560 --> 00:02:17.310
- It seems like its pretty
prevalent here among the kids,

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:21.410
among the adults. Its like
almost every family gets

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:22.330
touched by it, it seems.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:23.163
- Yeah.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.850
- So how does that effect you when you go

00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:27.893
to parties, when you
socialize? Stuff like that.

00:02:27.893 --> 00:02:31.030
- I don't. I stay at the house.

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:34.580
The most I ever do is go
to one of my cousins house

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:39.010
or go to my boyfriends house
because I'm not the party type.

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.720
- So you're avoiding it all?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.710
- Yeah.

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.577
- That's probably a smart move.

00:02:43.577 --> 00:02:46.010
And what's your plan after school?

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:50.240
- After I graduate high
school, I'm going to the

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.150
nursing college in Hazard.
They have a very good

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:56.930
nursing college and
that's my main interest

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:57.990
right now. Its getting through school

00:02:57.990 --> 00:02:59.540
and having a good life.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:02.530
- Good for you. And your
long term plan would be

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:03.830
to get away from this region?

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:07.070
- Yeah. Like just to get
away from all the drugs.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:11.460
I know its all over
the state but you know,

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:15.480
I can go on my own and not
have to have the choice

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:17.790
of either going down the wrong path

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:20.801
and messing my life life up.

00:03:20.801 --> 00:03:23.000
Because its all I've ever been around

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:24.950
- Yeah. Yeah you've seen it first hand

00:03:24.950 --> 00:03:25.806
- Yeah

00:03:25.806 --> 00:03:28.690
- What the ending result is. Are any of

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:30.880
your family members working?

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:31.713
- No

00:03:31.713 --> 00:03:33.220
- They're all just like
collecting money off

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.070
the government and

00:03:34.070 --> 00:03:37.333
- Yeah. Buying drugs and stuff with it.

00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:42.320
- Well its great that you're
steering clear of all that.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.933
That's a beautiful thing for you.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:47.830
How many kids would you say in your class

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:50.623
have the same attitude you do?

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:53.862
- About 50% of them.

00:03:53.862 --> 00:03:58.130
- 50%, that's good.
And then what about uh,

00:03:58.130 --> 00:03:59.180
you know college is expensive,

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.500
I don't know how much
money your family has.

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.570
- Yeah, um,

00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:05.400
they have a thing in
the state of Kentucky.

00:04:05.400 --> 00:04:07.740
If you're adopted, or in foster care,

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:09.400
you can go to college for free as long as

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.032
its in the state.

00:04:11.032 --> 00:04:11.865
- Oh really?

00:04:11.865 --> 00:04:12.698
- Yeah.

00:04:12.698 --> 00:04:13.531
- So that will help you out?

00:04:13.531 --> 00:04:15.170
- Yeah, a lot. Tremendously.

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:16.320
- That's a great thing.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.023
- So I mean, do you,

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.540
how do you view this, this region?

00:04:25.540 --> 00:04:29.790
You have lashes seem to be so affected

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:32.295
by drugs and unemployment.

00:04:32.295 --> 00:04:33.128
- Yeah

00:04:33.128 --> 00:04:37.377
- You see that, you are a smart
girl it seems. How do you..

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.270
Do you talk with your
friends about like what

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.130
the prospects are of staying here or

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:44.910
doing drugs or anything like that?

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:47.776
- Um, I've had a few friends

00:04:47.776 --> 00:04:50.290
that already took their own path

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:52.433
but they finally got their way back.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:56.043
And a lot of people getting on employment,

00:04:56.043 --> 00:04:58.920
(indistinct chatter)

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:02.363
but sometimes they just want
to buy other stuff with it.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:05.710
- How bad does it get in high school?

00:05:07.991 --> 00:05:08.824
- There's..

00:05:08.824 --> 00:05:10.410
- How serious is the drug problem I mean

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.630
- They even get to where they bring it

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:13.743
to school and sell it,

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:16.193
it's bad.

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:20.160
- In their families,

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.810
they have the same situation you do.

00:05:22.810 --> 00:05:24.210
It's in their families, it's what they've,

00:05:24.210 --> 00:05:25.860
it's the role models they've had.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.533
What's been your favorite
memory in your 16 years?

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:37.830
- Having my little
niece and nephew around.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:39.360
- Yeah, you have a couple

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:44.190
small, you have a sister
and a niece that uh,

00:05:44.190 --> 00:05:47.740
- Um, I have a niece and a nephew.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:48.630
- Oh, a nephew

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:49.793
- Yeah, and.

00:05:49.793 --> 00:05:51.160
- This is your,

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.840
- She's my niece, my older sister had her

00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:56.680
and her little brother Brandon

00:05:57.740 --> 00:06:02.740
and her mother took the
same path as our real mother

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:06.470
because she wanted her attention
so bad when she was little.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:11.097
- So your mom kind of takes
care of you, your niece

00:06:11.097 --> 00:06:11.930
- And my nephew

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.430
- And your nephew, and you guys
are all obviously drug free

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.980
and avoiding everyone that is

00:06:16.980 --> 00:06:17.813
is using right?

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:19.763
Good for you.

00:06:21.040 --> 00:06:22.435
So what are the best and
the worst things about

00:06:22.435 --> 00:06:24.163
living in that (inaudible)

00:06:24.163 --> 00:06:26.043
- The uh, good thing is

00:06:26.043 --> 00:06:31.043
like the scenery that you can
see all over like the fall

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.020
and I say about the only
bad thing going around here

00:06:34.020 --> 00:06:36.030
is the drug usage

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:40.223
and all that like young kids to adults.

00:06:42.689 --> 00:06:44.767
- Can you even envision staying here

00:06:44.767 --> 00:06:46.350
and trying to find a job and all that

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:47.415
or is it's just hopeless?

00:06:47.415 --> 00:06:48.248
- It's just hopeless.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.640
- It's a shame coz it's such
a lovely part of the country.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:53.810
- Yeah,

00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:55.142
- But it's just been destroyed,

00:06:55.142 --> 00:06:55.975
- Absolutely

00:06:55.975 --> 00:06:57.570
- The lack of employment and drugs

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:01.250
and your mom must be very proud.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:04.643
- Yeah, she is very ecstatic with me.

00:07:06.343 --> 00:07:09.997
- Like you see people in
your family, I mean what..

00:07:11.430 --> 00:07:13.066
They going through like depression

00:07:13.066 --> 00:07:16.410
and jail time and all kinds
of stuff like this right?

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.740
- Yeah,

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:20.423
- So that's such a great
warning sign for you to just uh,

00:07:20.423 --> 00:07:21.440
- Just steer clear

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.273
- Steer clear

00:07:23.269 --> 00:07:24.990
You have the scare straight program

00:07:24.990 --> 00:07:26.300
right in your own

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.133
living room.

00:07:27.133 --> 00:07:27.966
- Yes

00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:29.980
- What do you think of this life?

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.930
I mean, what do you think the
future is for (indistinct)

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:38.070
- I'd say if the people that
want help actually gets it

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:42.610
and sticks to it, this
could be an amazing place

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:45.660
but if they continue on the
path they're on there's no hope

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:48.680
for none of them.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:51.590
- Yeah, and what do you think
the most important lesson

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:54.210
you've learnt in your 16 years has been?

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:57.183
- Don't do drugs, like that's it,

00:07:57.183 --> 00:07:58.890
just don't do drugs no matter

00:07:58.890 --> 00:08:00.890
how much you get peer pressured in

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.430
trying to do them just don't do it.

00:08:03.430 --> 00:08:04.480
- That's a great one,

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:06.573
all right Selena,

00:08:06.573 --> 00:08:07.960
well thank you so much
for sharing your story

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:08.793
- You're welcome

00:08:08.793 --> 00:08:09.810
- And I wish you the
best of luck in college

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.166
and the rest of your life.

00:08:11.166 --> 00:08:12.210
- Thank you

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.490
- You're on the right
track, I'm proud of you

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:15.323
- Thank you

